{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Regression Interaction Term.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Regression Interaction Term.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"regression interaction term regression interaction term","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Regression Interaction Term.md","fileName":"Regression Interaction Term.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Regression Interaction Term","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 18:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Regression Model Development]] · [[Linear Model Design and Contrasts]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Regression Model Development","Linear Model Design and Contrasts","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Regression Interaction Term.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Regression Interaction Term.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"regression interaction term regression interaction term","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Regression Interaction Term.md","fileName":"Regression Interaction Term.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Regression Interaction Term","heading":"Regression Interaction Term","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A regression interaction term represents a relationship in which the effect of one explanatory variable depends on the level of another. It is commonly formed as a product while retaining the corresponding lower-order terms.\n\nOnce an interaction is included, the lower-order coefficients cannot be interpreted as universal effects. Estimates become stratum-specific combinations of coefficients, so unplanned interaction searches can both inflate false positives and make the model difficult to communicate.\n\nThe source constructs interaction columns by multiplying existing design-matrix columns. In R formula syntax, `type:leg` adds only the product terms, while `type*leg` expands to both main effects and their interaction.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Regression Model Development","Linear Model Design and Contrasts","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Regression Interaction Term.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Regression Interaction Term.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"regression interaction term regression interaction term","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Regression Interaction Term.md","fileName":"Regression Interaction Term.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Regression Interaction Term","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf]]\n\n[[dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Regression Model Development","Linear Model Design and Contrasts","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}